---
title: Loop 3 corrected — gate inserted, ranking split, failure paths added
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor H as Human
    participant AI as AI
    participant G as Elpi gate
    participant B as Booker
    participant A as Actor
    participant C as Critic
    participant DB as SQLite
    participant AL as Aleph / SWI

    Note over H,AI: loop 1 runs CONCURRENTLY with loop 3,<br/>not around it — else the queue stalls between gigs

    rect rgb(31,45,59)
    Note over AI,DB: read before proposing
    AI->>B: what needs doing
    B->>DB: query archetypes, refused set, capability table
    DB-->>AI: existing shapes + prior verdicts
    end

    rect rgb(59,31,31)
    Note over AI,G: THE GAP IN YOUR LOOP 3 — nothing crossed this edge
    AI->>G: actor schema + prediction + falsifiable_by
    G->>DB: composition_sig in refused set?
    alt refuse
        G-->>DB: verdict refuse, reasons
        G-->>AI: revise once, then escalate
    else queue
        G-->>H: requires_booking capability claimed
        H-->>G: approve / deny
    else book
        G->>DB: verdict book
    end
    end

    G->>B: approved composition only
    B->>DB: construct capability record from claims
    B->>A: gigStart, caps record passed by value

    rect rgb(45,35,51)
    Note over A,C: actors and critics are deterministic code.<br/>no model call below this line
    alt onFinish
        A-->>B: result
        B->>C: verify
        C-->>DB: mechanical verdict — parsed / tests / diff bounds
    else crash
        A-->>B: fault class
        B->>DB: crash fact + retry_index
        B->>AL: disposition/3 ?
        AL-->>B: reset (closed-world default) / preserve / drain
    else budget_exceeded or starved
        A-->>B: budget signal
        B->>DB: gig_outcome, no crash fact
    end
    end

    B->>AI: ping, gig closed
    AI->>DB: subjective rank — stored BESIDE the critic verdict,<br/>never instead of it

    rect rgb(31,59,45)
    Note over DB,AL: Aleph trains on the DETERMINISTIC label.<br/>the AI rank is a feature, not the target.<br/>disagreement between them routes to the human.
    DB->>AL: outcomes, offline cadence
    AL->>H: induced candidate rules
    H->>G: approved rules only
    end

    Note over AI,DB: the proposer never grades its own work unopposed —<br/>otherwise the loop closes and it learns to feel good
